1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,800
The generator has three windings, 120° apart.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,900
Each phase voltage, Vph, is 254 V.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:16,300
Between two phases you measure the distance between the arrow tips.

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:22,900
Half of it is Vph · cos 30°, which is Vph · √3/2.

5
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,100
Two halves: the twos cancel out.

6
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,400
VL = √3 · Vph.

7
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,900
254 V times 1.732 is 440 V.

8
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:40,900
That is why 440 V, and why √3 is in every three-phase formula.
